      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is what I thought in my first patch set fixing b/132766803 on Chrome OS, but we definitely saw this condition happening during CTS and crashing the system server (b/133367806).\n\nThis netid here comes directly from netd, not from ConnectivityService. For netd dns/connect events and tcp stats, the netid comes from the socket mark of the socket associated with the event.\n\nI am not sure what exactly cause netd to emit dns/connect events earlier than ConnectivityService being registered as a service, but I could definitely believe it to be the case.",
