      "writtenOn": "2019-07-04T02:30:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No I don\u0027t have any follow up change to address this TODO.\n\nThis TODO was based on a quick conversion with lorenzo@ a couple of years ago about incorporating this whole class into ConnectivityService (or as a child class owned by ConnectivityService) instead of as a stand alone service (the initial design that was chosen before I joined). The main benefits would have been simpler interaction between both and less boilerplate (no Parcelable, ...).\n\nActually the whole NetdEventListener should be folded into Netd binder interface now that NetworkManagementService has been migrated to Binder.\n\nI don\u0027t think this TODO is relevant anymore if no more works on legacy metrics is planned. Especially if netd events logging is migrated to some other event uploader/collector, the metrics side of this file will pretty much disappear. Note that DevicePolicy will still need this service to do dns/connect logging as a separate consumer.",
      "parentUuid": "bf3903ab_86ae1ea4",
